    "# 🐴 Week 5 – Functions: The Training Routines\n",
    "\n",
    "Welcome to Sunny Valley Riding Ranch! You've reached the **Training Hall of Perfection** – a place where training routines are developed once and can be reused for all horses. This week you'll learn the three **types of training methods**:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Your Mission:**\n",
    "- Master **function definition** with `def`\n",
    "- Control **parameters** for flexible training\n",
    "- Learn **return values** for training results\n",
    "- Understand **docstrings** for the training manuals\n",
    "\n",
    "**Developed once, applied forever!** The power of functions awaits..."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📚 Training Method 1: Function Definition – The Training Plan\n",
    "\n",
    "**What it is:** A function is a reusable training block that you define once and can call again and again.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The structure of a function:**\n",
    "```python\n",
    "def training_name(parameter1, parameter2):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Description of the training\"\"\"\n",
    "    # Training code\n",
    "    return result  # Optional: return a result\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Step-by-step explanation:**\n",
    "1. **`def`** – The command that starts the function definition\n",
    "2. **`training_name`** – A unique name for your training\n",
    "3. **`(parameter)`** – Training variables (optional)\n",
    "4. **`:`** – Ends the function definition\n",
    "5. **`\"\"\"Docstring\"\"\"`** – Training manual (very important!)\n",
    "6. **Indented code** – The actual training code\n",
    "7. **`return`** – Returns the result (optional)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why so useful:**\n",
    "- 🎯 Reuse training routines instead of rewriting them\n",
    "- 🔍 Organise and structure training\n",
    "- ⚡ Fix errors in one place\n",
    "- 🎲 Break complex training into small parts"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🏇 Training Method 1b: Calling Training – The Key to Application\n",
    "\n",
    "*Defining* a training routine isn't enough – it also has to be *called*! Calling is its own topic with important rules.\n",
    "\n",
    "### With and without parentheses\n",
    "\n",
    "**With parentheses `function()`:** The training is executed! The parentheses tell Python: "Run this function now".\n",
    "\n",
    "**Without parentheses `function`:** The training is NOT executed! You are only referencing the function object – nothing happens.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Calling with parameters\n",
    "\n",
    "When calling, you pass **arguments** in the parentheses: `function(argument1, argument2)`. The order must match!\n",
    "\n",
    "### From argument to variable\n",
    "\n",
    "**When calling:** You pass an **argument** (e.g. `\"Anna\"`)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Inside the function:** This becomes a **variable** with the parameter name (e.g. `name`)\n",
    "\n",
    "The parameter is a **placeholder**. When called, Python replaces it with the passed value – which is then available as a variable inside the function."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# With vs. without parentheses\n",
    "def greet_ranch():\n",
    "    \"\"\"Greets visitors at the riding ranch\"\"\"\n",
    "    print(\"Welcome to Sunny Valley Riding Ranch!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# WITH parentheses: function is executed\n",
    "print(\"=== With parentheses greet_ranch() ===\")\n",
    "greet_ranch()\n",
    "\n",
    "# WITHOUT parentheses: only a reference, nothing happens\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Without parentheses greet_ranch ===\")\n",
    "print(\"Type:\", type(greet_ranch))\n",
    "print(\"(The function was not executed!)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Argument becomes variable: step by step\n",
    "def greet_rider(name):  # \"name\" is the parameter (placeholder)\n",
    "    \"\"\"Greets a rider by name\"\"\"\n",
    "    # Inside the function, \"name\" is now a variable with the passed value!\n",
    "    print(f\"Inside the function: name = '{name}'\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Hello {name}!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# When calling: \"Anna\" is the argument\n",
    "print(\"=== Call: greet_rider('Anna') ===\")\n",
    "greet_rider(\"Anna\")  # → name becomes \"Anna\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Call: greet_rider('Max') ===\")\n",
    "greet_rider(\"Max\")  # → name becomes \"Max\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-5",
